{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DJt1EjPWb2KtdpNHRUn1Vo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-folder, local-first personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty â€” and, on top of that, a \"Mission Control\" for AI-trio-driven R&D. Grounded claims:\n\n- **Purpose:** A private GTD-style task/project manager. Plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, plus `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) are the single source of truth â€” no database, no syncing, everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`.\n\n- **What it ships (core):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) does the same operations and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`. A daily 5 AM health-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity and every endpoint.\n\n- **What it does (R&D surface):** Beyond tasks, it manages \"trio\" R&D work (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Each project is a thin full-width row with an auto-generated, **cached** summary; one trio run = one **session** with an in-place expandable summary (when Â· what-was-asked Â· doc links Â· token/time effort) rather than a separate page; brownfield-discovered history is treated as first-class.\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\":** Real interactive **ConPTY terminals** (via optional `pywinpty`), per-session **git-worktree isolation**, a durable session registry, a stacking draggable window manager, stage handoffs (build sessions execute on the most-recent plan set), and a runnable deliverable **preview** on an ephemeral port hard-guarded â‰  8777.\n\n- **Constraint it holds:** Python **stdlib-only**, with exactly one declared exception â€” `pywinpty`, imported lazily in `pty_manager.py` only, as an optional `[terminal]` extra that degrades gracefully if absent. `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this.\n\n- **Status:** The declared deliverable is the running `anchor_gui.py` itself. v3 was built by Foreman on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v3` (all 10 waves green, 529 tests passing) but is **not yet merged to master or deployed** â€” the live `:8777` service still runs the v2 surface.\n\nNote: the last two bullets lean on session memory (test counts, merge status); everything else is grounded in the checked-in `CLAUDE.md` and the project's frozen planning docs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20210,"cache_read_input_tokens":20573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20210},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d3a237f-8ea5-4488-a2cf-bc4edece1740","uuid":"ab52762f-a4ca-48bd-823a-fbd847b56251","request_id":"req_011CbyGs3NifMuPH6WT5Nmbw"}
